  "title": "Queen Tamar of Georgia",
  "summary": "Tamar of Georgia was the first queen regnant of medieval Georgia, formally titled King to assert her sovereign authority. Presiding over the Georgian Golden Age from 1184 to 1213, she expanded her realm across the Caucasus, defeated regional rivals at Shamkor and Basiani, and fostered a cultural flourishing that produced Shota Rustaveli's epic poetry.",
